WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.520
GA is about to begin.

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.760
I often get asked what GA stands for

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.850
but, to be honest, I don't know.

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:08.230
Shall I tell you?

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.990
Tomokane-san, you know?

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:10.940
Come here.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:11.390
Okay.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:12.520
Whisper, whisper.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:13.780
Oh, I see!

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.390
Sorry, Noda-chan.

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:54.900
That's my pencil.

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:57.790
Did you drop this gold brush?

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:01.170
Or this silver one?

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:07.030
Neither... that's not even silver.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:09.360
Then is it this tiny stub pencil?

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.180
That's the one! 
That's my pencil!

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.890
You are an honest person.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:17.420
So take your pencil and 
these two as well.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:18.920
But return them soon, okay?

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.440
Can't you just pick up the pencil
and return it, Princess Norinkonto?

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:26.360
But this one is different
from our school pencils.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:27.090
Oh, it is!

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.440
Like maybe it's easier to use?

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.070
It's really short so...

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:32.450
Oh, well...

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.620
I bought this pencil

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.400
before the entrance 
exams for this school.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:38.930
Oh yeah, we had one
 of those, didn't we?

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:39.800
A practical exam?

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:42.040
It's God's pencil!

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:48.850
<b>God's Pencil</b>

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:54.070
Welcome.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:02:59.240
What is it?

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.220
What are you looking for?

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.280
Um, a #2 pencil.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:03.960
A pencil?

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:04.540
Yes.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:08.600
I- I have a rough sketch exam tomorrow!

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.860
What should I do!

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.870
<b>Pencils</b>

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:11.330
Without a pencil I won't

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:13.600
be able to take the exam!

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:14.180
Just wait a second.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:19.480
I have just the one for you.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.270
Found it!

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.580
Here.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.820
They certainly seem like 
some very old pencils.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:29.200
Of course they do.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.620
After all, these are the 
time-honored pencils

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:36.450
used by the God of Studies, 
Sugawara no Michizane.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:37.300
What!

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.330
Are these pencils really that amazing?!

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:40.290
Of course!

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:43.220
On an exam, I'm sure 
these will come in handy.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.990
Um, but it's an art exam...

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:50.690
...and that's how this pencil 
was passed down to me.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.690
You mean sold.

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:52.700
In all likelihood, that 
old woman successfully

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:54.720
peddled off some old school supplies.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.080
You said it.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:59.410
Ahhh this is why Kisaragi is so cute!

00:03:56.080 --> 00:04:06.320
<b>Pet, pet</b>

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:00.580
You probably think

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:03.330
"weighing opinions" involves scales.

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:04.680
I- It's not like that.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.090
The pencil really worked!

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.580
In the Open Campus Rough Sketch Class

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:12.830
Open Campus

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:10.020
I received the lowest score of "D"

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.570
and was told that passing 
the entrance exam

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:12.830
would be very difficult...

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:19.340
Day Before The Exam

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.340
But the day before the exam,

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.290
I went through 20 of these pencils

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.340
and improved a lot!

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:21.050
There, there. You tried really hard.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:22.340
<b>Pat pat</b>

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:22.340
<b>Pet pet</b>

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:22.910
<b>KLONK!</b>

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:24.550
The number one thing you

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:26.050
suddenly leave class to go buy:

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:28.350
40 yen per page, Kent Paper!

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:28.850
<b>BAM!</b>

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:30.420
When you use it make sure you use a mask!

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:32.850
Sweet smelling fixative!

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:33.350
<b>Fwoosh!</b>

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:34.840
The two-dimensional 
battlefield upon which

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:35.970
white and black struggle!

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:37.330
Brutus Dessin!

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:42.160
You ended with "N"! Kisaragi loses!

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:45.000
GA shiritori is harder 
than you'd think.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.500
Hey, what are you doing?

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.260
This is clean up time, isn't it?

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:53.440
Yes, one second. 
I'm almost done.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.070
You're just planning 
on meeting up with your

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:57.000
3rd year tech student 
boyfriend after this anyway.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.890
Ew, what? How did you know!

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:00.320
How could I not?

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.880
I've been obsessed with 
you this whole time.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.310
Forget about that guy.

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:05.550
After all, compared to him, I...

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:06.410
Noda-chan!

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:09.220
Please stop playing with the scenery
outside and let's clean up.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:11.130
Hey, how are you?

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:13.190
What a day.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:15.400
I haven't seen Onaga around recently.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:16.520
What happened to him?

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.230
I heard he was eaten by 
a stray cat yesterday.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:20.230
Again?!

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:23.630
It's about time they 
installed a sturdier fence.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:26.350
We'd better be careful, too.

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:27.510
Are you serious?!

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.540
What? Kisaragi, you were sleeping 
in the video room again?

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:34.190
Well, since it was after P.E.,

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:35.370
I was out for about five minutes.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:36.750
Hey, I bought you some-

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:37.950
Oh, you're sleeping.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:41.700
I had a dream where I was
being chased in a Greek temple

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.730
by a Kore sculpture 
with an Archaic Smile.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:44.450
Really?

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:47.480
But Alexander the Great saved me.

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:47.960
Stop.

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:51.630
Probably because we were watching

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:54.470
The Unjust War of Greek Art

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:54.470
"The Unjust War of 
Greek Art into Hellenism"

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:56.950
Especially when we're sleeping lightly,

00:05:56.950 --> 00:06:00.430
things that we hear end up
 in our dreams, don't they?

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:02.890
Now listen closely, Tomokane.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:06.080
This is a story about a
young girl who attempts

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:07.800
to master the path of art.

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:10.750
Looks like the princess 
is up to something again.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:13.770
My name is Tomokane

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:17.760
I am a freshman 
student in Art School.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:27.050
Who the heck do you think you are?

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:30.080
Just give up or leave already.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.390
Hey, what's going on!

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:33.200
Oh, crap!

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:34.670
What was that?

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:39.410
Thank you very much for saving me.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:42.150
Your art supplies have been destroyed!

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:44.800
It's okay. I'm used to it.

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:48.240
If you hang out with me,
you'll get bullied too.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.010
I can't just leave things as they are.

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:52.160
I came to this school in search

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:55.810
of an underground organization 
hidden within the art world.

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:58.030
Why so suddenly?

00:06:58.150 --> 00:06:59.460
My brother was

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:02.800
killed by a gang called 
the "Hidden Arts".

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:05.760
He entrusted me with this brush
to remember him by!

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:07.790
Someday, I'll become

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.310
an even greater artist
 than my brother!

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:15.180
<b>Ooooh</b>

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:11.550
You've had such a heart 
wrenching past,

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:14.910
and yet you reveal all of this 
to someone you just met!

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:19.210
This is our classroom.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:23.190
Oh, look who decided 
to show up after all.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:25.660
Kisaragi-san, I hear 
you're the only one

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:27.460
wha hasn't been able to 
turn in her assignment.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:30.930
If you don't hurry up and 
paint it, class will be over.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:34.870
<b>He he he he...</b>

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.250
Don't pay any attention to them.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:34.040
I'll help you with your assignment.

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:34.870
But...

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:38.200
My art supplies aren't usable anymore.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:41.870
All I have left is scissors and glue.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:43.910
There's no way I could paint anything.

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:45.110
Don't worry.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:47.150
Art isn't made from tools.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:48.620
It's made from expression!

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:50.730
Noda-chan, would you like some fruit?

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:51.630
Yeah, how did you even get

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.750
frozen mandarins, Kisaragi?

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.120
<b>Woo hoo!</b>

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.100
All right, it’s done!

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.850
Damn, she finished it.

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:00.890
It's none of that girl's business.

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:03.880
What's finished? Show us.

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:08.340
What? Oh it's just a paper collage.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:13.140
A piece unsuited for a dignified 
art school like GA.

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:14.410
It's not "just" a paper collage.

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:16.220
Did you not notice the smell?

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:17.330
What?

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:18.780
Now that you mention it,

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:20.910
there's this refreshing citrus scent...

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:21.870
That's right.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:23.190
The orange color of that

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.220
piece is not simply orange color,

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:27.430
She pasted mandarin peels

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:31.220
<b>Blam!</b>

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:29.540
to produce a unified work of art!

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:30.400
No way!

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:34.520
And this water-like freshness,

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:36.230
A vivid landscape of orange

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:37.550
is spreading out before me,

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:40.220
sensed not only in sight,
 but in smell!

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:42.600
What? What happened to you, Masa?

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.800
Mandarins are delicious.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:47.750
She has succeeded in producing

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.870
a "natural" orange color that paints and

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:52.980
pigments alone cannot produce.

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:55.200
So you noticed.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.210
So, everything went 
according to her plan!

00:08:58.090 --> 00:08:59.670
Namiko-dono, Noda-dono,

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:02.040
We cannot even approach her 
feet in terms of skill.

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:03.850
Up until now,

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:05.800
I had never seen such an honest

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:07.990
and overflowingly playful piece of art.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:12.600
To have made Kyouju admit that much...

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:13.900
This is our loss.

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.460
You're a frightening woman.

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:18.470
And just like that,

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:20.600
the story of this incident, 
splendidly resolved by Tomokane,

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:22.610
became known throughout GA 
in the twinkle of an eye.

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:25.020
Where is this voice coming 
from? The heavens?

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.340
Yo Yo.

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:33.080
<b>Blam!</b>

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:29.260
Are you that freshman "Tomokane"

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:30.750
everyone's been talking about?

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:33.080
I'm here to test that 
famous hand of yours.

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:35.950
Ehh! A weird Kansai 
upperclassman appeared!

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:37.220
I challenge you

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:42.780
to a single match duel in 
plaster pencil of Gattamelata!

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:44.930
Know the strength of upperclassmen!

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:48.300
Amazing!

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:49.970
A level of detail that

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:52.130
depicts every muscle and blood vessel!

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:53.660
This is no sketch!

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:56.570
It's like he's been 
brought back to life!

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:58.030
No matter how good Tomokane-san is,

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.280
there's no way anyone 
could beat this...

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:01.190
Interesting!

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:04.110
I'll show you my true strength!

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.320
Bang, thump

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:12.690
Take this! The Gattamelan 
I drew at full power!

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:14.190
Hmph! Insolent!

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:19.480
It's sloppy, has stray lines 
and the balance is weird.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.190
I think the victor is clear.

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:24.200
Tomokane wins this match.

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:24.970
All right!

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:26.340
Tomokane wins!

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.590
<b>Tomokane's Drawing</b>

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.590
<b> Aa-san's Drawing</b>

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:30.350
Professor, is there something 
wrong with your eyes?

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:31.960
Even though she's your student,

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:32.980
you can't play favorites!

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:34.540
Like you said, Awara's drawing,

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:38.980
<b>Boo! Boo!</b>

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:36.940
so like a photograph, 
is a splendid piece of work.

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:39.060
However, you can sense

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:40.910
a throbbing heartbeat in

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:42.720
every rough line in Tomokane's sketch.

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:45.260
It has a mysterious appeal 
that shakes the soul.

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:47.670
This is Tomokane's originality

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:50.130
and is an essential innate 
ability for every artist.

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:53.950
T- that's... unbelievable!

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:56.470
How can my masterpiece 
lose to some infant's-

00:10:56.470 --> 00:10:57.950
You just don't get it.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:00.180
Art isn't a skill.

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:17.150
Zzzzz Zzzzz

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:02.390
It's an expression of your soul.

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:03.910
It looks like writing 
with your left hand and

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:06.150
writing with your right hand 
are totally different after all.

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:08.910
In its own way, this is an 
interesting piece of calligraphy.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:10.580
"Skillful unskillfullness".

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:17.120
Eat Ramen while it's hot.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:12.440
Even things that look childish at first

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.340
have a unique character.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:16.520
The upperclassman admitted her loss.

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:19.170
I'm done. I've lost.

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:20.790
I've completely lost.

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:21.590
Aa-san.

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:23.310
<b> Meanwhile</b>

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:22.920
Meanwhile...

00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:25.570
I see.

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:27.040
She must be quite skilled

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.830
to have defeated Awara.

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:30.100
Should it please you,

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:31.320
while it is early,
 perhaps it is time to act.

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:32.600
You're right.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.650
It's a little early, but let's use him.

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:38.530
Understood, Tono.

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:42.720
So the "Hidden" begins to move.

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:44.760
This could be the beginning 
of a civil war.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.110
We, the Renaissancers, must be ready.

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:46.680
Ma'am.

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.590
Unaware of the dark movements 
in the shadows of GA,

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:51.940
Tomokane steadily continues 
along her path as a student

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:53.990
in order to become an artist.

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:55.990
It really is amazing, isn't it?

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:58.060
There isn't a person in this school

00:11:58.060 --> 00:11:59.820
who doesn't know you, Tomokane.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.500
Quit it, Kisaragi. 
You're embarrassing me.

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:03.360
But as it is,

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:06.100
I haven't found a single 
lead on the "Hidden".

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:08.700
Tomokane-san, about that...

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:11.510
Actually, I am a member

00:12:11.510 --> 00:12:12.990
of that Hidden organization.

00:12:12.990 --> 00:12:13.880
Are you serious?!

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.890
Could it really be that

00:12:15.890 --> 00:12:17.510
you haven't noticed until now?

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:18.850
Even though I'm wearing glasses:

00:12:18.850 --> 00:12:20.630
the symbol of the Hidden.

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:23.580
I had no idea.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:25.920
Or rather, this is the first 
time I've heard about any symbol.

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:29.430
I even put the Hidden's 
mark on my notebook...

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:32.930
I thought it meant that 
that was the back cover.

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:34.980
So then, if you can defeat me,

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.200
I shall reveal to you information

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:38.240
about the leaders of the "Hidden"!

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:39.690
Interesting!

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.420
What a gripping turn of events!

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:43.110
Dong

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:42.480
First bell?

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:44.490
But why is it coming from the sky?

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:46.020
Unfortunately, that's 
all the time we have!

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:47.230
To be continued next week!

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:48.470
What is this?!

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:52.680
Oh! You're awake.

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:56.690
<b>Grin</b>

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:56.690
Is that a new paintbrush?

00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:59.020
I purchased it for half price

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:00.200
at the supply shop yesterday.

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:02.160
Oh Tomokane, you're awake.

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:03.640
Hurry up and get ready.

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.200
We're in Art Room 1.

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.540
You're the leader of the 
Hidden organization!

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:13.920
Looks like she figured something out.

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:19.500
GA: Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:24.110
Oh, are you here to look around?

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:28.560
Um, this is GA1, GA's freshman class.

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:31.780
The staff room is around 
the corner to your left--

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:34.750
You want to know what GA means?

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:40.060
Oh, I remember!

00:13:40.060 --> 00:13:41.550
It means "Gambare Atashitachi"! 
(Let's go us!)

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:42.740
Ahh! Don't mind her.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:44.640
She's a complete airhead!

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:51.580
But that "GA" slip-up this 
morning was something.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:55.630
Tomokane told me with 
such confidence so I...

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:56.410
That's right.

00:13:56.790 --> 00:13:59.910
"GA" stands for Geijutsuka A-class.

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:01.590
Art is A-class.

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:03.410
A-class? So that means?

00:14:03.410 --> 00:14:05.190
That's right.
 There is also a B-class.

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:08.790
Geijutsuka is divided into two 
classes of Art and Music.

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:11.390
The classroom over there 
is the Music class.

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:12.860
Wow, you're right.

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:15.200
The class sign says "GB-1"!

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:18.610
I mean, Music is an 
art form, too, right?

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:24.870
So, "GA" doesn't stand for 
"Geijutsuka Art Design"?

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:26.890
So none of you noticed.

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:29.580
<b>Today's Studies</b>

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:29.070
Today's studies.

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:31.080
Sketching

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:31.080
Pencil sketching

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:30.900
Pencil sketching

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:37.310
<b> Hard to Soft</b>

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:34.180
Using pencils from 9H to 6B,

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:37.320
express the shading and feel 
of a material accurately.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:39.720
That won't do Noda-chan.

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:40.260
Huh?

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:43.390
You're too dark from 
the very beginning.

00:14:43.390 --> 00:14:44.410
Huh?

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:46.240
Aren't you supposed to start

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:48.380
with the dark shading first?

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:50.580
If you start with 6B your drawing will

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:51.770
turn out completely black!

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:54.590
Also, you need to differentiate between

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:56.820
the texture of the apple and the plate.

00:14:57.310 --> 00:14:59.360
So should I use 6H for the plate?

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:00.980
This skinny, light one?

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:03.900
Actually, if you start 
with such a hard pencil

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.780
the paper will scratch when you erase.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:08.380
Well, for starters,

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:09.470
why don't we just try pencils

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:10.700
from the outside one by one?

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:14.170
This is just like...

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:15.410
what was it?

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:16.790
With a knife and a fork...

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:18.880
Table manners for a full 
course western meal?

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:19.600
Yeah, that!

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:20.630
<b>Errrg</b>

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:23.540
I can't handle it anymore!

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:25.370
Noda-chan exploded!

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:27.770
Before coming to GA,
 I had no idea that

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:29.960
there were so many types of pencils.

00:15:30.190 --> 00:15:33.310
In practice, 5 or 6 gradients 
of shading is fine,

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:34.960
So we gradually find a few

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:36.540
that we find easy to use...

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:37.380
True, true.

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:42.600
For me, I only ever use a 
single HB for sketching.

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:43.910
Otherwise it's a pain.

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:45.340
Just one?

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.460
How do you make different textures?

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:50.340
Pencil pressure?

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:52.930
She forces her way 
through everything...

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:58.440
<b> Bzzzzz</b>

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:00.230
What!

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:00.840
A fly.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:04.830
The fly landed on the 
tissue sketch subject!

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:06.730
If it changes the shape of the tissue

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:08.580
I'll have to redo it completely!

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:11.310
Is there some way we can 
get rid of just the fly?

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:13.190
Wait a sec, I have just the thing.

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:15.880
Found it! Here, chopsticks.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.690
What are you expecting from me...

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:27.870
Kisaragi-chan, do you 
have any kneaded eraser?

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:29.400
Mine's all black.

00:16:29.810 --> 00:16:31.910
Ahh, well, here, take half of mine.

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:32.630
You actually got it!

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:34.010
Thanks!

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:36.300
Wow. New ones stretch a lot.

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:40.700
You're not going to erase anything?

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:43.890
For example, when sketching tissues,

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.870
it is necessary to express both

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:48.110
a soft and delicate motif and

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:51.020
a solid, hard motif.

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:54.760
Tomokane-dono's tissues look like iron.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.530
Kisaragi's box looks like a sponge.

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:00.640
Character is apparent even 
in drawings, isn't it?

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:03.000
Maybe this time I'll try it 
with just one 6B pencil!

00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:07.350
Ah, finished.

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:10.130
Wha! The side of my 
hand is totally black!

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:17.810
Huh?

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:19.010
Hey!

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:21.060
Kyouju-san and... Noda-chan?

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:22.090
Looks like it.

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:23.680
Are you also headed to the

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.960
middle school art equipment 
room as well, Kisaragi-dono?

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:27.770
Huh? Can you tell?

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:31.390
We were just taking over 
a box just like yours.

00:17:31.390 --> 00:17:33.750
Don't let your guard down against them.

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:34.500
Yeah.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:35.530
Okay?

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:39.460
There's some kind of demon 
so be careful, okay?

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:40.620
Give her a break, you two.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:43.260
Kisaragi is really troubled 
by how to respond.

00:17:43.810 --> 00:17:46.340
I wonder if there's a scary 
teacher or something?

00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:49.330
Or maybe they were just 
trying to trick you.

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:51.050
I'm opening it.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:55.530
Huh? It doesn't look like 
there's anything, does it?

00:17:55.530 --> 00:17:57.560
I'll just put this here.

00:17:57.560 --> 00:17:58.880
Here, Kisaragi, yours too.

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:00.270
Oh, thanks.

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:04.590
Oh, there's a room further back as well.

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:09.500
What happened, Kisaragi?

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:14.260
<b>Hug me!</b>

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:14.260
 Warning just painted!! 
It's a trap.

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:17.820
Kisaragi! Stop! 
It's a trap!

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:20.310
I'll hug you meooow!

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:25.550
Boo hoo

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:23.730
Hurry up and wash it off.

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:25.030
Yup. As expected.

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:26.650
GA!

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:31.560
100%!

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:33.830
... Yes, it is.

00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:36.620
You're high energy with 
everything, aren't you?

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:39.300
Little do you know,

00:18:39.530 --> 00:18:42.580
I've just recharged to 100%!

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:44.490
She somehow seems so powerful!

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:46.100
<b> Invincible!</b>

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:45.320
Invincible!

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:49.880
I'm drinking the same drink 
so why do I feel defeated?

00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:50.940
Now, now.

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:54.930
I'll never lose!
 I'm 200%!!

00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:55.740
Cheater!

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:58.100
Hey, the university vending 
machine has more-

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:01.190
Then I have 100,001%.

00:18:58.680 --> 00:18:59.680
Krssh

00:19:01.190 --> 00:19:02.450
What?!

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:05.690
I've walked into a conversation 
that makes no sense.

00:19:10.070 --> 00:19:11.900
Kisaragi, wanna go to the lounge?

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:14.210
Oh, I'm going to go home early.

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:16.050
I thought I'd buy some pencils.

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:16.930
Pencils?

00:19:17.110 --> 00:19:17.980
At the school supply store?

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:19.780
At the local stationary store

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:21.520
I was talking about in class.

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:23.520
I thought I'd say thanks to

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:24.970
the old woman while I was there.

00:19:25.170 --> 00:19:26.050
Thanks?

00:19:26.050 --> 00:19:29.990
Yes. "Thanks to your 
Divine Pencil I passed!"

00:19:29.990 --> 00:19:32.450
Ohh, is that so..

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:33.830
Kisaragi!

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:35.950
There, there.
 Off you go.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.720
Erasers.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.720
Old Looking Stationary Store

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:42.590
Excuse me, are you open?

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:44.060
Welcome.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:47.330
Uhm, is that elderly woman...

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:49.330
Elderly woman? Oh.

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:51.960
My grandmother passed 
away two months ago.

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:54.660
Oh, is that so.

00:19:54.990 --> 00:19:57.010
Did you have some 
business with her?

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:58.480
Business, or rather...

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:01.830
Last year, I bought these 
pencils from her...

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:03.270
Like this.

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:05.360
You bought this?

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:08.510
Yes. Before my entrance exams. For art.

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:10.880
Hah, is that so.

00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:13.890
So you were tricked by 
my grandmother, as well.

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:15.230
One second.

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:18.640
These, right?

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:22.760
I feel bad that you used them 
till they were so small.

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:26.650
My grandmother would occasionally 
bring out old supplies

00:20:26.650 --> 00:20:30.000
and make up great stories 
to tease customers.

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:33.850
Although, there weren't many 
people who believed her...

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:39.580
You're probably one of the few 
that were tricked by her.

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:42.970
By the way, I was tricked into buying

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:46.550
"The world's first HB 
pencil used by Aristotle".

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:47.960
You believed her?!

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:48.610
<b> Can't talk about other people.</b>

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:48.630
Yup.

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:51.140
And sure, while it may seem like

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:53.150
what my grandmother did 
was a practical joke...

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:58.100
These days, even students 
don't buy pencils much.

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:01.440
I think maybe she only 
said those things

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:03.770
to people who cared about pencils.

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:08.110
You seem like you might 
be a little clumsy.

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:12.920
These pencils will look after 
you during your exams.

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:14.120
What about you?

00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:17.450
I thought maybe you came 
to this store because

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:20.000
you believed in the 
influence of a pencil.

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:23.790
Yes.

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:26.300
Well, since you came
 all the way here,

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:27.630
I'll give these to you.

00:21:28.560 --> 00:21:30.400
Although, this is all that's left.

00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:32.710
I- I- I couldn't take it.

00:21:32.710 --> 00:21:33.620
It's fine, it's fine.

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:35.910
But...

00:21:35.910 --> 00:21:38.310
I'm happy that you 
came all the way

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:40.050
to this store, and besides,

00:21:40.050 --> 00:21:43.270
If you're doing art then
you'll need more pencils anyway.

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:45.520
I probably won't ever use them.

00:21:51.020 --> 00:21:53.980
T- then, half! Half! Halfsies!

00:21:54.810 --> 00:21:57.140
<b> The Next Day</b>

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:00.740
She's sharpening her pencil!

00:22:00.740 --> 00:22:02.410
One from that store?

00:22:02.410 --> 00:22:05.190
I bought this one from the supply shop.

00:22:02.950 --> 00:22:08.940
It's dangerous to look away 
while using a box cutter.

00:22:05.190 --> 00:22:06.360
Really?

00:22:06.790 --> 00:22:08.260
Didn't you go to the store?

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:09.880
Or did they not have any?

00:22:11.510 --> 00:22:13.210
They're kind of special.

00:22:13.210 --> 00:22:14.930
So I thought I'd save them

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:17.340
for about two and a 
half years from now.

00:22:17.340 --> 00:22:18.650
Two and a half years from now?

00:22:21.140 --> 00:22:22.040
Yes.

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:26.050 --> 00:23:27.520
Let's play tag!

00:23:27.520 --> 00:23:29.190
Let's play tag!

00:23:29.190 --> 00:23:30.690
Prohibited during class.

00:23:30.690 --> 00:23:32.260
Make sure it's only during breaks.

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:34.080
Make sure we agree on rules.

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:36.260
They're always weirdly different 
depending on where you're from.

00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:40.050
Tag Collage

00:23:36.860 --> 00:23:39.230
The art club sure seems active!
